  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">North Kordfan Food Security and Livelihood for vulnerable rural community</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve livelihoods and food security for vulnerable households in 5 rural villages within the Sheikan locality in North Kordofan state, tapping into the farming or pastoralist background, and the small-scale business skills, of the internally displaced families in the area.  It will:

&#x2022;	provide access to agricultural inputs and services (seeds, equipment and training) for 350 farmers;
&#x2022;	give 550 vulnerable households access to drinking water, through the provision of equipment and storage facilities, and the establishment of water management committees;
&#x2022;	improve livestock quality for 200 households, through vaccination campaigns and the provision of vaccines and treatment;
&#x2022;	establish functioning saving and loan groups.</narrative>
  </description>
